    <div class="alpheios-lex-entry" lemma-id="n58124" body-key=""><b><span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">κνήθ-ω</span></b> , later form of <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">κνάω</span>, <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>A.</b><i>scratch</i>, 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ὡς λέγεται, κνήθειν οἶδεν ὄνος τὸν
					ὄνον</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					<u>AP</u>
					12.238.8
				</span></i>
			 (<i><span class="en">
				Strat.
			</span></i>), cf. Moer.<i><span class="en">
				p.234
			</span></i> P.:—
				Med.
			, <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">κνήθεσθαι εἰς τὰς ἀκάνθας τὰ
				ἕλκη</span>
			<i>to get</i> one's sores <i>scratched</i>, <i><span class="en">
				Arist.
				<u>HA</u>
				609a32
			</span></i>. </div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense3"><b>2.</b>
			
				Pass.
			, <i>itch</i>, Paul. Aeg.<i><span class="en">
				6.60
			</span></i>; 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">κνηθόμενοι τὴν ἀκοήν</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					<u>2 Ep.Ti.</u>
					4.3
				</span></i>
			; <i>to be provoked</i>, <i><span class="en">
				Arist.
				<u>Pr.</u>
				957b15
			</span></i>.</div>
